    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205205829936_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Fleet Mechanic",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-06-05\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nPRIMARY PURPOSE: Ave Maria University is seeking a dependable, hands-on Fleet Mechanic to join our Operations team. This position is responsible for performing preventive maintenance, inspections, and minor repairs on a diverse fleet of landscape equipment, golf carts, utility vehicles, aerial lifts, and other small motorized assets. The Fleet Mechanic will also support parts inventory management, vendor coordination, and light welding or fabrication work as needed. This is an excellent opportunity for an early-career mechanic to grow within a mission-driven university environment.  ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:   Perform scheduled preventive maintenance on landscape equipment, golf carts, lifts, utility vehicles, and other fleet assets in accordance with manufacturer specifications and university standards. Diagnose and complete minor mechanical, electrical, and hydraulic repairs to maintain fleet readiness and minimize downtime. Conduct routine fleet inspections and document findings; maintain accurate service records within the university’s computerized maintenance management system (Asset Essentials). Develop and maintain a preventive maintenance schedule for all fleet assets, ensuring compliance with safety and regulatory requirements. Manage parts inventory levels, place orders, and coordinate with vendors to ensure timely availability of parts and supplies. Perform light welding, fabrication, and modification work to support equipment repairs and minor operational projects. Maintain a clean, organized, and safe shop environment in accordance with OSHA standards and university policies. Communicate equipment status, repair timelines, and any safety concerns to the Fleet Supervisor in a timely manner. Support other Operations team functions as needed, including occasional assistance with Facilities and Grounds projects. EDUCATION: High school diploma or GED equivalent required. EXPERIENCE: One to two (1–2) years of hands-on experience in equipment maintenance, small engine repair, or a related mechanical trade. CERTIFICATION: Valid Florida driver’s license with a clean driving record. KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES:   Minimum Qualifications Basic knowledge of gasoline and small diesel engines, electrical systems, hydraulics, and drivetrain components. Ability to read and interpret equipment manuals, parts diagrams, and service bulletins. Ability to lift up to 50 pounds and work in outdoor Florida conditions, including heat and humidity. Preferred Qualifications Experience servicing golf carts (gas and electric), zero-turn mowers, string trimmers, blowers, and similar landscape equipment. Small engine certification or manufacturer-specific training (e.g., Stihl, Toro, Club Car, E-Z-GO). Diesel engine repair experience (light- to medium-duty). Basic MIG/stick welding and fabrication skills. Experience using a CMMS or work order system to log and track maintenance activities. Familiarity with OSHA safety standards for shop and equipment operations. Key Competencies Safety-First Mindset – Consistently follows safe work practices and identifies hazards proactively. Reliability – Demonstrates strong attendance, punctuality, and follow-through on assigned tasks. Problem-Solving – Approaches mechanical issues methodically and resourcefully. Communication – Provides clear, timely updates on work status and escalates issues appropriately. Teamwork – Works cooperatively with Grounds, Facilities, and other Operations staff. Continuous Improvement – Willing to learn new skills, pursue certifications, and adopt better maintenance practices. PHYSICAL SKILLS AND ABILITIES: This position requires regular standing, walking, bending, kneeling, and lifting up to 50 pounds. Work is performed both indoors (shop environment) and outdoors in varying weather conditions.   WORKING CONDITIONS: The role involves regular exposure to noise, fumes, oils, chemicals, and moving mechanical parts. Appropriate personal protective equipment (PPE) will be provided and is required at all times. Ave Maria University is a Catholic institution of higher education. Ave Maria University makes employment decisions in a manner that is consistent with federal, state and local law. All information included in any application must be truthful and accurate.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9205198181107_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Director of Marching Band",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-05-12\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nPRIMARY PURPOSE: The Director of Marching Band is responsible for the creation, implementation, leadership, and administration of the university’s marching band program and related instrumental ensembles. This part-time position provides artistic, educational, operational, and strategic oversight while supporting the mission of Ave Maria University and enhancing campus spirit, student engagement, and institutional visibility. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:   Program Development Establish and implement the vision, structure, and operational framework for the university marching band program Develop strategic plans for program growth, recruitment, retention, and sustainability Create traditions, performance standards, and organizational culture for the program Student Recruitment and Retention Recruit qualified student musicians through outreach to high schools, music educators, and prospective students Collaborate with admissions, athletics, and campus leadership on recruitment initiatives Develop retention strategies and student leadership opportunities Instruction and Performance Conduct and direct marching band rehearsals and performances Direct additional ensembles including concert band, jazz band, pep band, and other instrumental groups as assigned Select music, coordinate drill design, and oversee show development Evaluate student performance and provide mentoring and instruction Administrative Management Prepare and manage annual operating budgets Oversee purchasing, inventory, equipment, uniforms, instruments, and facilities Coordinate travel, scheduling, contracts, and event logistics Ensure compliance with university policies and safety procedures Personnel Management Recruit, supervise, and evaluate assistant directors and student leaders as assigned Institutional Engagement Represent the university at performances, outreach events, and community functions Collaborate with university departments to support institutional events and student engagement initiatives EDUCATION: Bachelor’s degree in Music, Music Education, Conducting, or related field. Master’s degree preferred.  EXPERIENCE: Minimum of 3–5 years of progressively responsible experience directing marching bands, concert bands, jazz ensembles, or related instrumental music programs, preferably at the high school or collegiate level. Experience with performance planning, rehearsal design, and event coordination.  CERTIFICATION:  N/A KNOWLEDGE, SKILLS AND ABILITIES:  Demonstrated success in marching band instruction and leadership. Strong organizational, communication, and administrative skills. Ability to work evenings and weekends, as needed. Experience in drill design, arranging, budgeting, and personnel supervision. Must support the University’s Catholic mission.  PHYSICAL SKILLS AND ABILITIES: Requires ordinary ambulatory skills sufficient to visit other locations. Ability to stand for extended periods. Ability to conduct rehearsals and performances outdoors in varied weather conditions. Ability to lift and transport equipment up to 30 pounds. WORKING CONDITIONS: Work is performed both indoors and outdoors with exposure to outdoor elements typical to our location in SW Florida; heat, humidity, rain, etc.   Ave Maria University is a Catholic institution of higher education. Ave Maria University makes employment decisions in a manner that is consistent with federal, state and local law. All information included in any application must be truthful and accurate.   The responsibilities and requirements listed above are not an exhaustive list of all that will be expected of this position; however, it is met to identify the general criteria for this position.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=70cb71c1-96f8-4956-8cce-ce625b0b2943&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201305005522_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing",
      "description": "Posted: 2025-08-27\n\nLocation: AVE MARIA\n\nAve Maria University seeks applicants for a full-time position in Nursing.  Applicants with a doctoral degree in Nursing are preferred.   A master’s degree in nursing is acceptable.  Applicants with a minimum of three years of clinical nursing experience, experience as a preceptor, or educator are preferred. Experience in simulation and clinical skills instruction and debriefing is desired. Certification in Basic Cardiac Life Support (BCLS) is required; certified instructors in Basic Cardiac Life Support (BCLS) are preferred. Knowledge of clinical practice, quality improvement, patient safety initiatives. and evidence-based care of multicultural populations are strongly preferred. Ideal candidates will possess expertise in Maternal, Pediatric, and/or Medical/Surgical Care, and will have the ability to teach a broad range of courses in nursing.   Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, three references willing to supply letters upon request, and a short statement relating the University’s Catholic mission to their philosophy of the curriculum as expressed in Ex Corde Ecclesiae . Questions should be directed to Dr. DiAnn Ecret, DiAnn.Ecret@avemaria.edu . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. The position is subject to final administrative approval. Those who received any graduate degrees from an institution outside the United States must provide a foreign course-by-course credential evaluation by an independent evaluation service that is a member of the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc. (NACES).  Find a full list of NACES members at http://www.naces.org/members.htm .",
      "department": ""
    },
